{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "Synthetic Substation Five Auxiliary Power Loss due to Torn Stress Cone Cable Fault",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "Auxiliary cable C-S05-07 at Synthetic Substation Five had a torn stress cone from excessive pulling force.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The 2021 installation report lists a maximum pull of 9.3 kN, exceeding the specified 6.8 kN limit.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "With breaker 52-R3 withdrawn for battery maintenance, no alternate station-service source could be switched online.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Later examination of the surge arresters found no discharge damage, eliminating the lightning flash as the trigger.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 01:33:02, a partial discharge of 265 pC ignited at the torn stress cone.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 1]
        },
        {
          "text": "By 01:33:04, the discharge had formed a carbonized track over the insulation surface.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 0]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 01:33:07, a phase-to-ground arc developed, melting the aluminum sheath around the splice.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5, 0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The arc engulfed the adjacent phase 15 ms later, creating a phase-to-phase short circuit in C-S05-07.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 5]
        },
        {
          "text": "Relay 51-07 channel P indicated 2,025 A; independent channel Q indicated 2,226 A; physical current was 2,150 A.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7]
        },
        {
          "text": "After an inverse-time delay of 28 ms, relay 51-07 issued a trip command to breaker 52-07.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Breaker 52-07 opened in 40 ms and lockout relay 86-07 operated, sealing the station service supply off.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "With breaker 52-07 open, the auxiliary transformer T-2 saw no voltage on its 12.47 kV side.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [10, 2]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 480 V station-service bus de-energized, dropping the ventilation fan and stopping the battery charger's AC input.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The charger's triac, with MT1 and MT2 in the input, commutated off at the next zero crossing because gate pulses stopped.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "During an 18-minute outage, the DC bus voltage fell from 125.0 V to 121.7 V at a current draw of 45 A.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [13]
        },
        {
          "text": "Transformer oil temperature rose 5.2 °C in 18 minutes, as obtained from the stated thermal time constant.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 01:51, a portable diesel generator was connected to the 480 V bus by a field crew, restoring auxiliary supply.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The damaged cable section was cut out and replaced with a new splice using a hydrophobic cold-shrink joint.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [7]
        },
        {
          "text": "A revised pulling procedure now requires a recording dynamometer and limits tension to 6.0 kN on all auxiliary cables.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 1]
        },
        {
          "text": "Relay 51-07 channel Q scaling was corrected; both channel P and Q now report the same fault current after calibration.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        }
      ],
      "distractor_seeds": [
        "A station battery charger output current is usually regulated by battery temperature compensation rather than load current alone.",
        "The neutral grounding of a 12.47 kV wye station service bus typically uses an impedance that limits ground fault current to 400 A.",
        "Triac terminal MT1 is often used as the reference point for the gate driver supply.",
        "Station service load lists include motor-operated switch chargers, breaker heaters, and panel lighting.",
        "Battery room ventilation exhausts hydrogen at the top of the room and has no relation to the AC distribution.",
        "A maintenance grounding set is installed whenever any worker enters the cable termination cabinet.",
        "The station's local area network carries control level messages and does not rely on auxiliary power after a UPS failure.",
        "Cable trays for I&C circuits must be separated from power cables by at least 300 mm, per synthetic construction practice.",
        "A 52a contact is used by the breaker to indicate the closed state to the station controller.",
        "An 86 lockout reset is required after any zone-interlocked protection operation, but the process is not tied to the charger.",
        "Fault recorders often use separate subcycle data from the relay's trip logic to time-stamp events.",
        "The SCADA control system can supervise fan-start interlocking without a live AC voltage by using battery-powered master stations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Synthetic Mesa Switching Station Auxiliary Power Loss from Excavation-Induced Cable Strike",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "A backhoe excavation for a new control building began without a utility locate at Synthetic Mesa Switching Station.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The as-built drawing listed no concrete slab over the duct bank, so the bucket struck the cable directly.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The standby generator's start controller had an open triac gate lead, eliminating automatic backup service.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Later insulation-resistance tests showed 200 MΩ on the other phases, ruling out pre-existing cable aging.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:22:33, the backhoe tooth crushed cable C-M7-22, forming a phase-to-ground arc.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 1]
        },
        {
          "text": "The arc's thermal jets vaporized the adjacent cable insulation, creating a three-phase bolted fault after 9 ms.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The total fault current reached 2,740 A on a 12.47 kV system, based on network calculations.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "The fault remained until breaker 52-1 tripped 82 ms later; no current-limit fuses were installed.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        },
        {
          "text": "Relay 51-1's channel N measured 2,612 A, while channel M indicated 2,928 A; physical current was 2,740 A.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 7]
        },
        {
          "text": "After 45 ms of definite-time delay, relay 51-1 issued a trip command to circuit breaker 52-1.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Breaker 52-1 opened, and lockout relay 86-1 operated, sealing the normal source in the tripped position.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The standby generator failed to start; its triac gate circuit remained open, so breaker 52-2 stayed open.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [2, 10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 480 V auxiliary bus remained deenergized, since neither normal nor generator source supplied it.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10, 11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The battery charger output ceased, and the DC bus decayed from 125.0 V to 118.6 V over 24 minutes.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer oil temperature rose 5.5 °C in the same 24 minutes, following the manufacturer's cooling curve.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The remote terminal unit lost AC-powered inputs and retained only battery-backed statuses for the 24-minute outage.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:46:33, an operator manually started the generator and closed breaker 52-2, reenergizing the 480 V bus.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [11, 12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The damaged cable section was replaced, and a reinforced concrete duct bank was constructed over the new route.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The triac gate wire on the generator start controller was reterminated and secured with a locking connector.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "Relay 51-1's metering channel M was recalibrated so that both N and M report the same current values.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        }
      ],
      "distractor_seeds": [
        "Duct bank installations typically require mechanical protection at least 900 mm below grade and warning tape above the conductors.",
        "A diesel generator's voltage regulator control loop usually uses a triac to fire the exciter field in both half cycles.",
        "The transfer switch logic has a time delay before closing the emergency breaker to allow the generator to stabilize.",
        "Ground resistance measurements for the station mat are taken on a clear day and are unaffected by the cable trench insulation.",
        "Relay testing uses a secondary injection set to apply current to the relay without energizing the main circuit.",
        "Protection CTs are specified with a C800 rating for low burden on high fault currents.",
        "The station's electrical dip charts list a conductor span's required sag based on ambient temperature.",
        "Control-room UPS batteries are sized for 2 hours, not for the station main battery's 8-hour rating.",
        "A phase sequence indicator verifies the order L1-L2-L3 before paralleling the emergency source to the load bus.",
        "Battery charger alarm bits are communicated over the station bus to the local controller even during a generator trip.",
        "Medium-voltage cable jackets are extruded with carbon black for UV protection where installed in open trays.",
        "Manual close of a breaker requires a control switch with trust position and a closing spring that has been charged."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
